EuclideanEnergy adapts Analysis/FunctionalSpaces/Sobolev/Euclidean/H1.lean.
The local formulation distinguishes the mass projection from an injective
embedding for an arbitrary measure and records the maximum product norm.
EuclideanTranslations adapts Euclidean/Translation.lean and
Euclidean/TranslationEstimate.lean from the same rellich-kondrachov source.
TranslationEnergyBound adapts Euclidean/TranslationEstimateL2.lean and
Euclidean/TranslationEstimateH1.lean. The closure argument is reduced to a
closed inequality in the ambient product of the two L² spaces.
LpZeroExtension adapts MeasureTheory/Function/LpSpace/Restrict.lean, reducing
the linearity proofs to pointwise indicator identities and preserving the
full Lp norm. The declarations remain in the project-owned Sobolev namespace.
ConvolutionSmoothing adapts Euclidean/L2Compactness/Smoothing.lean. It uses
the local extension isometry directly, avoiding duplicate L² representatives.
ConvolutionApproximation adapts Euclidean/L2Compactness/Approximation.lean.
The local probability proof is supplied explicitly, rather than registered
as an instance with uninferable analytic arguments.
SmallProbabilityKernels adapts Euclidean/L2Compactness/Kernels.lean.
SmoothedTranslationBound adapts Euclidean/L2Compactness/TranslationIntegral.lean.
SmoothingCompactnessCriterion adapts Euclidean/L2Compactness/FrechetKolmogorov.lean.
Its fixed-kernel input is the local corpus-based CompactConvolution theorem.
EuclideanRellich adapts Euclidean/Rellich.lean. Its compact C¹-family
corollary also follows OpenAI CubicSieve/RadialWindows.lean. The local
unit-ball proof applies the constructed kernels and gradient translation
estimate directly, without raised elaboration limits.
CompactCutoffCharts adapts the finite cutoff cover from OpenAI
Eisenstein/CompactEnergyFamilies.lean and combines it with the local
Euclidean Rellich theorem and exact restricted quotient measure charts.
TheCubicQuotientHasASmoothAtlas adapts Möbius coordinate charts and deck
transitions from OpenAI CubicSieve/RowCaps.lean, coordinates from
MeanSquare/TransformedColumns.lean, and manifold instances and smooth
projection from Eisenstein/SmoothTests.lean.
SmoothTestsOnTheCubicQuotient adapts full support from OpenAI
MeanSquare/TransformedColumns.lean and smooth test density from
Eisenstein/SmoothTests.lean, using the locally constructed finite quotient
volume and smooth atlas.
HyperbolicActionPreservesEnergy adapts the differential norm and cotangent
energy identities from OpenAI GaussSum/ReflectedBranches.lean. It uses the
local inversion derivative and Bruhat decomposition.
ComplexWeakGradientGraph adapts the complex distributional gradient graph
and Hilbert norm from OpenAI MeanSquare/SourceTransfer.lean. Distributional
injectivity and Schwartz density come from the installed mathlib.
TheCubicDirichletForm adapts the descended energy density from OpenAI
GaussSum/ReflectedBranches.lean and polarization from Eisenstein/DirichletForm.lean.
It uses the actual smooth quotient atlas and the locally proved invariance
of the hyperbolic cotangent energy.
TheCubicEnergyGraph adapts the smooth gradient graph from OpenAI
CubicSieve/RadialWindows.lean and its Hilbert completion from
CubicSieve/PaddedPassage.lean. Its norm identity uses the actual quotient
Dirichlet form and fundamental-domain measure constructed locally.
LocalizingTheCubicEnergy adapts the cutoff Leibniz estimate and chart mass
comparison from OpenAI Eisenstein/LocalCutoffs.lean, and the Hilbert energy
bound from CubicSieve/PaddedPassage.lean. It uses the locally constructed
distributional gradient space and actual quotient measure charts.
LocalizingTheCompletedCubicEnergy adapts continuous extension of the energy
and mass localizations from OpenAI CubicSieve/PaddedPassage.lean. The norm
bounds are discharged by the locally proved cutoff and measure estimates.
TheCubicGradientIsClosable adapts reverse localization, cutoff faithfulness,
and gradient closability from OpenAI Eisenstein/VariationalLaplacian.lean.
It uses the local cutoff cover and actual weak-gradient localization.
CompactCubicEnergyLocalizations adapts real and imaginary Rellich localization
from OpenAI CubicSieve/ReopenedFibers.lean. It uses the local Euclidean Rellich
theorem and explicit Borel transport, then extends compactness by density.
CompactRestrictionOfTheCubicEnergy adapts the finite-chart estimate from
OpenAI Eisenstein/CompactEnergyFamilies.lean. Restriction uses the corpus
Lp cutoff map, and compact domination uses its canonical-system theorem.
TheCubicVariationalLaplacian adapts the coercive variational solution and
resolvent graph from OpenAI Eisenstein/VariationalLaplacian.lean. The local
mass embedding is proved injective and dense; these facts discharge the
closed, densely defined, nonnegative self-adjoint operator construction.
GreenIdentityOnTheCubicQuotient adapts finite chart partitions and weighted
Schwartz integration by parts from OpenAI CubicSieve/RadialProfiles.lean.
The local proof uses the actual restricted quotient measure and explicit
Euclidean coordinate-vector values for the weighted divergence identity.
TheCubicLaplacianHasItsCoordinateExpression adapts global Green identities
from OpenAI Eisenstein/CoordinateLaplacian.lean and support-local equations
from MeanSquare/UnitRows.lean. Density of the locally constructed energy
core identifies the coordinate equation with the actual operator graph.
HyperbolicAxisLaplacian adapts affine axis differentiation from OpenAI
MeanSquare/UnitRows.lean and the axis expression from Eisenstein/SmoothSummands.lean.
HyperbolicLogarithmicHeight adapts quadratic height calculus from OpenAI
CubicSieve/TwistedProfiles.lean, QuadraticSieve/SpatialDerivatives.lean, and
Eisenstein/SmoothCuspCutoffs.lean. Its actual row-height identity uses the
locally proved upper triangular row-energy formula.
HyperbolicHeightProfiles adapts logarithmic profile differentiation and
finite axis sums from OpenAI Eisenstein/SmoothCuspCutoffs.lean. The local
proof uses the actual row-height identity and the local axis calculus.
TheCubicCuspBarrier adapts the invariant cusp construction and compact
defect from OpenAI Eisenstein/CuspHeight.lean, and smooth transitions from
Eisenstein/SmoothCuspCutoffs.lean. Its local finiteness input is the local
bounded-row theorem; the chart reconstruction is from SmoothTests.lean.
TheCubicCuspProfileEquation adapts the locally finite row-profile equation
from OpenAI Eisenstein/CuspHeight.lean. The proof uses the locally checked
height calculus and finite-sum axis identities.
TheCubicBarrierPotential adapts the potential, coordinate equation, and
scalar ground-state square completion from OpenAI Eisenstein/BarrierPotential.lean.
All barrier and Laplace inputs are locally constructed and checked.
TheCubicExteriorCoercivity adapts compact testing, ground-state integration,
and density extension from OpenAI CubicSieve/CutoffOrders.lean. The actual
barrier equation, support-local Green identity, and compact restriction
are all supplied by locally checked modules.
TheCubicSpectralPencilIsFredholm adapts spectral estimates from OpenAI
Eisenstein/FredholmAlternative.lean. Closed range and finite kernel use
the existing corpus ConstitutiveCompactCofinalFusion theorem; finite
cokernel follows from self-adjointness and orthogonal decomposition.
TheCubicMeromorphicResolvent adapts finite-nullspace splitting, analytic
regular inversion, and the actual resolvent identities from OpenAI
Eisenstein/MeromorphicResolvent.lean. Its Fredholm and variational
inputs are supplied by locally checked modules.
CharacterEquivariantCubicCuspProfiles adapts high-cusp uniqueness and
character-equivariant profile sums from OpenAI Poisson/LatticeEnvelopes.lean.
The height-product obstruction and cusp stabilizer are locally checked.
CubicIncomingHeightProfiles adapts logarithmic powers from OpenAI
CubicSieve/TwistedProfiles.lean and cutoff differentiation and defect
regularity from Eisenstein/SmoothCuspCutoffs.lean and SeedDefects.lean.
SmoothCubicCuspSeeds adapts the locally finite height-profile sums and
seed equations from OpenAI Eisenstein/SmoothCuspCutoffs.lean,
SeedDefects.lean, and FundamentalDomain.lean. Local finiteness uses
the locally checked integral-row bound and actual spatial chart.
CubicCompactHeightProfiles adapts the bounded profile map and entire
L² defect family from OpenAI Eisenstein/CompactProfiles.lean. Its
high-cusp uniqueness and quotient measure are locally constructed.
CompactSmoothCubicDefects adapts high-cusp vanishing, compact support,
and smooth chart transport from OpenAI Eisenstein/TransformedColumns.lean,
SmoothTests.lean, and SeedHeight.lean. The quotient and height bounds
are supplied by locally checked modules.
TheCubicIncomingResidue adapts the actual forcing correction and its
spectral residue from OpenAI Eisenstein/MeromorphicResolvent.lean.
The entire forcing and meromorphic resolvent are locally checked.
